# Verify org/team vs CRM super group/group

Two parallel hierarchies. Do not conflate names or assume roles transfer 1:1.

## Vocabulary

| Side | Parent | Child | Membership / roles |
|------|--------|-------|--------------------|
| **Verify** | **Organization** (`verify_organization`) | **Team** (`verify_team`) | `verify_team_user_link.user_role` |
| **Legacy CRM (LC)** | **Super group** (`obj_m_group`, `is_super_group`) | **Group** (`obj_m_group`) | `obj_m_mglink.client_type` (`Owner` / `Admin` / `Normal` / …) |

Rough parallel: **org ≈ super-group bucket**, **team ≈ group** — related, not identical objects.

## How the pieces relate

`verify_organization` has **no FK to a group or super group**. CRM rows and Slack links point **at** the org.

| Relation | How it is stored |
|----------|------------------|
| **Verify team → org** | `verify_team.organization_uuid` → `verify_organization.obj_uuid` (many teams per org) |
| **CRM group → org** | Child `obj_m_group.organization_id` = org uuid — **usual** place members/admins live |
| **CRM super group → org** | Same `organization_id` on the super-group row — **optional** (often `NULL`, e.g. IBM Supergroup) |
| **CRM group ↔ super group** | **No direct parent FK.** For Slack, join via `slack_super_group_link`: child `organization_id` = link.`verify_organization_uuid` → `super_group_uuid` |

**Both are possible:** a Verify org can be referenced by child groups, by a super group, or by both. Slack workspaces pair **org + super group** on one `slack_super_group_link` row (org may be null on older links).

```text
Verify:     organization ──< team
                 ▲
                 │  organization_id (optional on super; usual on child groups)
                 │
CRM:        [super group] ··· via Slack link ··· [group] ──< mglink ── member
                 ▲                                    ▲
                 └──── slack_super_group_link ────────┘
                       (workspace: super_group_uuid + verify_organization_uuid)
```

## Slack link tables (`ray_integration`)

| Table | Links | Org? | Team? |
|-------|-------|------|-------|
| **`slack_deltaray_link`** | Slack user ↔ LC **member** (`member_uuid` = `obj_m_member.obj_uuid`) | **No** | **No** (Verify team). `slack_team_id` is the **Slack workspace** id, not Verify team |
| **`slack_super_group_link`** | Slack workspace ↔ CRM **super group** + Verify **organization** | **Yes** (`verify_organization_uuid`) | **No** |

Deltaray is **member-only** (unique `member_uuid`). Workspace org/super-group context comes from `slack_super_group_link`, not from the deltaray row.

## Practical notes

- Org-billed Document MT uses `verify_organization_uuid` as `client_id`.
- Quote Admin/Owner: workspace super group **or** any active Admin/Owner LC group under the workspace Verify org (e.g. IBM Slack App). Default group (`obj_m_member.groupid`) is unused; inactive mglinks do not count.
- Verify team role ≠ CRM `client_type`. Unrelated Straker CRM Admin ≠ customer workspace org Admin.
- Prefer workspace `verify_organization_uuid` / linked super group for workspace gates; without workspace link, quote admin gate denies.

See also: [docs/verify-org-vs-crm-groups.md](../../docs/verify-org-vs-crm-groups.md).
